Imports:
  - Types:
      - Logger
    From: BrowserKit/Sources/Common/Logger

Annotations: |
  This cell is the engine-agnostic abstraction boundary between the browser and its rendering
  engine: `Engine` creates views/sessions, `EngineSession` is the per-tab handle a client drives
  (load, navigate, reload, tracking-protection controls, zoom, find-in-page), `EngineView`
  renders one session, and `EngineSessionDelegate`/`EngineTelemetryProxy` are the callback
  surfaces a client implements to observe a session. The one concrete WebKit-backed
  implementation, in this same target's own webview subdirectory, is out of scope for this cell
  — this cell documents only the contract a client of the engine, or a future alternate engine
  implementation, must honor.

---

"Engine()":
  location: Engine.swift
  annotations: |
    Factory for engine views and sessions, plus process-lifecycle and data-clearing hooks. Only
    one `EngineView` is created per engine, but many `EngineSession`s can exist concurrently
    (one per tab).
  methods:
    "createView() -> view:EngineView": |
      Create a new view for rendering web content.
    "createSession(dependencies: EngineSessionDependencies) -> session:EngineSession": |
      Create a new per-tab engine session.

      `dependencies`: session-specific configuration (webview parameters, reader-mode delegate,
      telemetry proxy)
    "warmEngine()": |
      Prepare the engine when the app moves to the foreground.
    "idleEngine()": |
      Release engine resources when the app moves to the background.
    "clearCaches()": |
      Clear cached web resources.
    "clearCookies()": |
      Clear stored cookies.
    "clearOfflineWebsiteData()": |
      Clear offline/website storage data.
    "clearTrackingProtection()": |
      Clear tracking-protection state.

"EngineSession()":
  location: EngineSession.swift
  annotations: |
    One browsing session; in practice, one per open tab.
  properties:
    "delegate -> EngineSessionDelegate?": |
      Receives navigation/loading/menu events for this session.
    "telemetryProxy -> EngineTelemetryProxy?": |
      Receives engine-agnostic telemetry events for this session.
    "isActive -> Bool": |
      Whether this session is currently being rendered.
  methods:
    "load(browserURL: BrowserURL)": |
      Load `browserURL` in this session.
    "stopLoading()": |
      Stop the current in-flight load.
    "reload(bypassCache: Bool)": |
      Reload the current URL.

      `bypassCache`: when true, fully reload from the origin instead of the cache
    "goBack()": |
      Navigate back in this session's history.
    "goForward()": |
      Navigate forward in this session's history.
    "scrollToTop()": |
      Scroll the page to the top.
    "showFindInPage(withSearchText searchText: String?)": |
      Show the engine's built-in find-in-page interaction, optionally pre-filled.
    "goToHistory(item: EngineSessionBackForwardListItem)": |
      Navigate to a specific back/forward-list entry.
    "currentHistoryItem() -> item:EngineSessionBackForwardListItem?": |
      The currently active back/forward-list entry.
    "getBackListItems() -> items:[EngineSessionBackForwardListItem]": |
      The back-navigation history list.
    "getForwardListItems() -> items:[EngineSessionBackForwardListItem]": |
      The forward-navigation history list.
    "restore(state: Data)": |
      Restore a previously saved session state (history, scroll position, zoom, form data).
    "close()": |
      Close the session and free its underlying resources.
    "switchToStandardTrackingProtection()": |
      Switch this session to standard tracking-protection strictness.
    "switchToStrictTrackingProtection()": |
      Switch this session to strict tracking-protection strictness.
    "disableTrackingProtection()": |
      Disable tracking protection for this session.
    "toggleNoImageMode()": |
      Toggle image-blocking mode for this session.
    "updatePageZoom(change: ZoomChangeValue)": |
      Adjust the page zoom level (increase, decrease, reset, or set to an explicit value).

"EngineView()":
  location: EngineView.swift
  annotations: |
    Renders the content of one `EngineSession`.
  methods:
    "render(session: EngineSession)": |
      Start rendering `session`'s content in this view.

"EngineSessionDelegate()":
  location: EngineSessionDelegate.swift
  annotations: |
    Callback surface for observing one `EngineSession`'s navigation, loading, and content-menu
    events.
  methods:
    "onTitleChange(title: String)": |
      The session's page title changed.
    "onLocationChange(url: String)": |
      The session's URL changed.
    "onHasOnlySecureContentChanged(secure: Bool)": |
      Whether every loaded resource came over an encrypted connection changed.
    "onProgress(progress: Double)": |
      Loading progress was updated.
    "onHideProgressBar()": |
      The progress bar should be hidden without animating (e.g. localhost navigations).
    "onNavigationStateChange(canGoBack: Bool, canGoForward: Bool)": |
      Back/forward availability changed.
    "onLoadingStateChange(loading: Bool)": |
      Loading started or finished.
    "didLoad(pageMetadata: EnginePageMetadata)": |
      Page metadata finished loading or was updated.
    "onErrorPageRequest(error: NSError)": |
      The session hit an error that should show an error page.
    "findInPage(with selection: String)": |
      The user chose "find in page" for the given text selection.
    "search(with selection: String)": |
      The user chose "search" for the given text selection.
    "onProvideContextualMenu(linkURL: URL?) -> menu:UIContextMenuConfiguration?": |
      Build a contextual menu for a long-press, optionally on a link.

      `linkURL`: the link under the press, if any
      `menu`: the menu to show, or nil to show none
    "onWillDisplayAccessoryView() -> view:EngineInputAccessoryView": |
      Choose the keyboard accessory view to show for this session (default or none).
    "adsSearchProviderModels() -> models:[EngineSearchProviderModel]": |
      Custom ad-tracking definitions for ads found on the current page.
    "requestMediaCapturePermission() -> allowed:Bool": |
      Whether camera/microphone capture should be allowed for this session.
    "onRequestOpenNewSession(session: EngineSession)": |
      A navigation requested a new session (e.g. a link opening in a new tab); the delegate must
      decide how to present it.

"EngineTelemetryProxy()":
  location: EngineTelemetryProxy.swift
  annotations: |
    Engine-agnostic telemetry sink; clients record these through Glean or any preferred backend.
  methods:
    "handleTelemetry(event: EngineTelemetryEvent)": |
      Record one engine telemetry event (navigation failure, error page shown, page load
      started/cancelled/finished, ads found/clicked on page).

"EngineSessionBackForwardListItem()":
  location: EngineSessionBackForwardListItem.swift
  annotations: |
    One entry in a session's back/forward navigation history.
  properties:
    "url -> URL": |
      URL of this history entry.
    "title -> String?": |
      Page title of this history entry, if known.

"BrowserURL(browsingContext: BrowsingContext, securityManager: SecurityManager, logger: Logger)":
  location: BrowserURL.swift
  annotations: |
    The only URL type `EngineSession`'s load method accepts, so loading a URL always goes
    through security-policy validation first.

    `browsingContext`: the context (source, target, and requested URL) to validate
    `securityManager`: policy consulted to decide whether the context may navigate; defaults to
    the standard security manager
    `logger`: diagnostic logger; defaults to the app-wide `Logger` singleton

    Algorithm:
    1. Ask the security manager whether the browsing context is allowed to navigate
    2. If not allowed, log it and fail to construct the value
    3. If allowed, store the browsing context's URL

"EngineSessionDependencies(webviewParameters: WKWebViewParameters, readerModeDelegate: WKReaderModeDelegate?, telemetryProxy: EngineTelemetryProxy?)":
  location: EngineSessionDependencies.swift
  annotations: |
    Session-specific configuration supplied when a new engine session is created.

    `webviewParameters`: engine-specific webview configuration
    `readerModeDelegate`: optional reader-mode event observer for this session
    `telemetryProxy`: optional telemetry sink for this session

"EngineDependencies(readerModeConfiguration: ReaderModeConfiguration)":
  location: EngineSessionDependencies.swift
  annotations: |
    Configuration that applies to the engine as a whole rather than to one session.

    `readerModeConfiguration`: global reader-mode configuration

